Backport HTTP/1.1 async streams with Connection: close from Drogon PR #2527:
https://github.com/drogonframework/drogon/commit/c9db379743f8a095b7a2a561b26fc1745628a453

Keep synchronous close-delimited streams unchanged: their send path in 1.9.7
only applies chunk framing to keep-alive responses. Async ResponseStream always
frames chunks, independently of whether the connection closes afterward.
Remove this patch when upgrading to a Drogon release containing the fix.

--- a/lib/src/HttpResponseImpl.cc
+++ b/lib/src/HttpResponseImpl.cc
@@ -529,7 +529,8 @@
         {
             // When the headers are created, it is time to set the transfer
             // encoding to chunked if the contents size is not specified
-            if (!ifCloseConnection() &&
+            if (version_ != Version::kHttp10 &&
+                (asyncStreamCallback_ || !ifCloseConnection()) &&
                 headers_.find("content-length") == headers_.end())
             {
                 LOG_DEBUG << "send stream with transfer-encoding chunked";
--- a/lib/src/HttpServer.cc
+++ b/lib/src/HttpServer.cc
